# A17.var06: second group member XTIME

Draft pending independent postrun review. The direct parent is accepted `A17.two_units.1.0.0`; no parent native run or checker was repeated. The child changes exactly `UnitGroupMember[TEACH-GROUP, TEACH-UNIT-2].XTIME` from 0.0 to 1.0. The 36-hour horizon, seed, two explicit units, aircraft, group and mission definitions, and PDESC are unchanged.

The single approved native attempt completed four native commands and two new pure checker stages with OS exit 0. The author checkers matched the predeclared 33-table/20-row/203-cell input, 33-table/38-row/387-cell export, byte-identical 60-line/52-timed physical log, and all 4,966 selected J07 group-report typed cells. In that selected report, only `FixedMissionResults.STOTD` changed from the accepted J07 group control value 0 to 1. The converter log has zero errors, warnings #108 and #126 only, and exact Input/Output/File paths within its 17-line grammar. These are author observations pending an unchanged independent recovered-copy replay and receipt-bound GO.

This is one source-bound reporting effect for the two-system group mission using the accepted `group.sxs` selection settings. It does not establish a general XTIME formula, a physical-timing change, unit-level mission rollup, other group sizes or assignments, GUI behavior, cross-engine parity, performance, all of A17.var06, or Issue 18 completion. The full-log equality and single-cell report change were frozen as hypotheses before native observation.

Full sealed replay requires the 66 prelaunch mandatory originals, the zero-native preflight originals, all native/PURE/transport originals, and byte-equal recovered run copies on the controlled host. Bulky model and report originals remain host-bound. Finite inert copies and their exact custody map will be added only after the independent postrun and publication gates. A published checkout alone will not establish a full sealed replay.

Publication becomes effective only after independent postrun GO, evidence-index closure, independent content review, catalog append, Git review, and merge.
